Q1)
  BEGIN
    SET threshold = 80%
    usage = GET_DISK_USAGE()
    IF usage > threshold THEN
        FIND log_files
        SORT log_files by size
        FOR each file DO
            ROTATE or COMPRESS file
            usage = GET_DISK_USAGE()
            IF usage <= threshold THEN
                BREAK
            ENDIF
        ENDFOR
        IF usage > threshold THEN
            DELETE oldest log files
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END
Set disk usage limit to 80%.
Check the current disk usage.
If usage exceeds 80%, find and sort log files.
Rotate or compress the log files to save space.
Check usage again.
If still above 80%, delete the oldest unnecessary logs.
Stop when disk usage becomes 80% or less.

Q2)
    BEGIN
    INPUT process_list with priority and burst time
    SORT process_list BY priority (highest first)
    WHILE process_list is NOT EMPTY DO
        SELECT process with highest priority
        ALLOCATE CPU to selected process
        EXECUTE process
        IF process is completed THEN
            REMOVE process from process_list
        ELSE
            UPDATE its priority
            ADD process back to process_list
        ENDIF
        SORT process_list BY updated priority
    ENDWHILE
    DISPLAY all completed processes
END
Input: Get processes with their priority and burst time.
Sort: Arrange processes based on priority, with the highest priority first.
Select: Choose the process having the highest priority.
Execute: Allocate CPU and execute the selected process.
Completion: Remove the process if it is completed.
Update: If it is not completed, update its priority and add it back.
Repeat: Continue until all processes are completed.


Q3)
    BEGIN
    SET total_RAM = 16GB
    SET host_reserved = 4GB
    SET available_RAM = total_RAM - host_reserved
    SET min_RAM = 2GB
    INPUT number_of_VMs
    FOR i = 1 TO number_of_VMs DO
        IF available_RAM >= min_RAM THEN
            ALLOCATE min_RAM to VM[i]
            available_RAM = available_RAM - min_RAM
        ELSE
            PRINT "Insufficient memory for VM[i]"
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR
    DISPLAY remaining available_RAM
END
Reserve 4 GB RAM for the host OS.
Calculate available RAM: 16 − 4 = 12 GB.
Each VM requires at least 2 GB.
Allocate 2 GB to each VM if enough memory is available.
Reduce available RAM after every allocation.
If memory is insufficient, display a warning.
Finally, display the remaining RAM.

