    BEGIN
    INPUT performance_required
    INPUT budget
    INPUT hardware_access
    IF performance_required = HIGH AND hardware_access = TRUE THEN
        SELECT Type_1_Hypervisor
        SET reason = "High performance and direct hardware access" 
    ELSE IF budget = LOW THEN
        SELECT Type_2_Hypervisor
        SET reason = "Low cost and easy setup" 
    ELSE
        SELECT Type_1_Hypervisor
        SET reason = "Better performance and resource utilization"
    ENDIF
    PRINT selected_hypervisor
    PRINT reason
END
Input requirements: Get performance needs, available budget, and hardware access.
High performance: If high performance and direct hardware access are required, select Type-1 hypervisor.
Low budget: If the budget is low, select Type-2 hypervisor because it is simpler and suitable for general use.
Default choice: If neither condition applies, select Type-1 for better resource utilization.
Display result: Finally, display the selected hypervisor and the reason for the selection.


Q5)
     BEGIN
    INPUT application_list

    FOR each app IN application_list DO
        CREATE resource group for app
        SET CPU usage limit
        SET memory usage limit
        ASSIGN app process to resource group
        MONITOR CPU and memory usage
        IF usage exceeds limit THEN
            REDUCE resource allocation
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR
    DISPLAY resource usage
END
Input: Get the list of applications running in the system.
Create resource group: Create a cgroup for each application to control its resources.
Set limits: Define maximum CPU and memory limits for each application.
Assign process: Place the application process inside its resource group.
Monitor usage: Continuously check CPU and memory consumption.
Control excess usage: If an application exceeds its limit, reduce its resource allocation.
Display usage: Finally, show the resource usage of the applications.













